            {
               "text": "### Images from Machu Picchu\n\nThese images are copyright for Machu Picchu and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMachuPicchu0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMachuPicchu0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Photo of the city of Machu Picchu, Peru. Photo taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the city (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Understanding the Multiplication Table (4 and 5) - In this text, we examine the relationship between triangles and mountains. (<htcite1>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite3>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite4>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMachuPicchu1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMachuPicchu1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Photo of the city of Machu Picchu, Peru. Photo taken on <htdate1>, during a visit to the city (<htcite5>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Modulating (Part III) - Continuing from the previous text, we see how the 'negative multiplication table' allows us to deepen our understanding of inclinations. (<htcite6>)</li><li>What do I need to build? - The question may seem complex, but the answer might be right around you. (<htcite7>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">3 / 3</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgMachuPicchu2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgMachuPicchu2', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Interior photo of the city of Machu Picchu, Peru. Photo taken on <htdate2>, during a visit to the city (<htcite8>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Modulating (Part III) - Continuing from the previous text, we see how the 'negative multiplication table' allows us to deepen our understanding of inclinations. (<htcite9>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
